window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-3353f8f8f4d90d76"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"projects-and-chats\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">项目与聊天</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>使用项目整理相关聊天，并为 ChatGPT 提供所需上下文。ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 <strong>Projects（项目）</strong>视图包含 ChatGPT 项目，以及连接到电脑文件夹的本地项目。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-project-or-start-without-one\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择项目，或不使用项目开始</h2> <p>如果一项工作会持续一段时间、需要产出多个结果，或依赖同一批文件和来源，就创建一个项目。如果工作自成一体、无需共享项目上下文，就直接开始聊天。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>使用项目把相关聊天、文件、指令和来源放在一起。同一个项目可以包含从 Chat 或 ChatGPT Work 开始的聊天。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-project-or-chat-without-one\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">选择项目，或不创建项目直接聊天</h2> <p>如果一项工作会持续一段时间、需要产出多个结果，或依赖同一批文件和来源，就创建一个项目。如果工作自成一体、无需共享项目上下文，就直接开始聊天。</p> <p>每个项目都有 <strong>Chats（聊天）</strong>部分，用来列出项目中的聊天；还有 <strong>Sources（来源）</strong>部分，用来放置上传的文件和已连接的上下文。项目指令适用于该项目中的所有聊天。ChatGPT 项目不能直接访问你电脑上的文件夹；如需使用这些资料，请上传文件或连接相应来源。</p> <p>无论选择哪种方式，都可以从项目中新建聊天来使用共享文件和指令，然后在 <strong>Chats（聊天）</strong>部分重新打开它。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex CLI 会把启动它时所在的目录视为当前聊天的项目。请在希望 Codex 使用的目录中运行 <code>codex</code>，或传入 <code>--cd &lt;directory&gt;</code>（<code>-C</code>）显式指定目录。CLI 不提供 ChatGPT 的 Projects（项目）视图。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>IDE 扩展会把 IDE 中打开的文件夹或工作区视为本地项目。在多根工作区中，请为当前聊天选择工作区根目录。该扩展不提供网页或桌面应用中的 ChatGPT Projects（项目）视图。</p> <p><a id=\"work-in-a-project\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"_4\">在项目中工作</h2> <p><strong>Projects（项目）</strong>视图把 ChatGPT 项目和本地项目集中在一处。ChatGPT 项目会在相关聊天之间保留项目文件和上下文。本地项目则允许聊天访问电脑上的一个或多个文件夹，例如一组源文件或一个代码库。</p> <p>每个不同目标都单独开一个聊天，让聊天中的消息和结果保持聚焦，同时由项目统一整理相关工作。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用在侧边栏显示多个项目、在主面板显示聊天。</p> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"work-in-a-project_1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">在项目中工作</h2> <p>ChatGPT 项目中的聊天可以使用相同的上传文件、项目指令和已连接来源。简单交流可以使用 Chat；较大的交付工作可以使用 ChatGPT Work；两者都会显示在项目的 <strong>Chats（聊天）</strong>部分。每个不同目标都单独开一个聊天，让消息和结果保持聚焦，同时由项目保留共享上下文。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"work-in-a-project-directory\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">在项目目录中工作</h2> <p>从应为聊天提供文件上下文的目录启动 Codex。使用 <code>/new</code> 为每个不同目标开始单独的聊天。Codex 打开时可使用 <code>/resume</code> 继续聊天，也可以运行 <code>codex resume</code> 恢复已保存的聊天。</p> <p>聊天会保留记录和启动时的工作目录，而 Codex 会读取当前工作树中的文件。请把长期有效的项目指引写入 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或提交到代码库的文档中，方便以后的聊天使用。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"work-in-a-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">在工作区中工作</h2> <p>打开应为聊天提供上下文的文件夹或工作区。每个不同目标都开始一个新聊天，然后从 <strong>Recent chats（最近聊天）</strong>中选择它以继续。同一项目中的聊天可以使用相同文件，但每个聊天都保留自己的对话记录。</p> <p>当前选择内容和打开的文件会为当前轮次提供上下文。请把长期有效的项目指引写入 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或提交到代码库的文档中，方便以后的聊天使用。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-project-threads\"></a> <a id=\"organize-projects-and-chats\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"organize-projects-and-tasks\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">整理项目与聊天</h2> <p>让正在进行的工作保持醒目，并把已完成的工作收纳起来：</p> <ul> <li><strong>固定项目</strong>，让它显示在侧边栏靠前的位置。也可以在 Projects（项目）视图中固定项目。</li> <li><strong>固定聊天</strong>：即使项目中出现了更新的聊天，也能让你经常返回的聊天保持醒目。</li> <li><strong>重命名聊天</strong>，使用能说明目标的简短标题，例如“Q3 发布简报”或“结账流程无障碍审查”。</li> <li><strong>搜索项目</strong>：从 Projects（项目）视图搜索。如果只记得过去聊天中的一句话或分支名称、却不记得标题，可从侧边栏打开 <strong>Search chats（搜索聊天）</strong>。搜索聊天没有默认快捷键，但可以在 <strong>Settings &gt; Keyboard Shortcuts（设置 &gt; 键盘快捷键）</strong>中为它指定快捷键。</li> <li><strong>归档聊天</strong>：工作完成后，从项目菜单中选择 <strong>Archive chats（归档聊天）</strong>，即可一起归档该项目中的聊天。</li> </ul> <p>固定项目或聊天不会添加上下文，也不会改变 ChatGPT 可访问的内容；它只会改变项目或聊天在侧边栏中的位置。</p> <p>如需恢复已归档的聊天，请前往 <strong>Settings &gt; Archived chats（设置 &gt; 已归档聊天）</strong>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"organize-projects-and-tasks-1\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"organize-projects-and-chats_1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">整理项目与聊天</h2> <p>让正在进行的工作保持醒目，并把已完成的工作收纳起来：</p> <ul> <li><strong>固定项目</strong>，让它显示在侧边栏靠前的位置。也可以在 Projects（项目）视图中固定项目。</li> <li><strong>固定聊天</strong>：即使项目中出现了更新的聊天，也能让你经常返回的聊天保持醒目。</li> <li><strong>重命名聊天</strong>，使用能说明目标的简短标题，例如“Q3 发布简报”或“结账流程无障碍审查”。</li> <li><strong>搜索项目</strong>：从 Projects（项目）视图搜索。只记得过去聊天中的一句话或分支名称、却不记得标题时，可使用 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> 搜索聊天。</li> <li><strong>归档聊天</strong>：工作完成后归档聊天。</li> </ul> <p>固定项目或聊天不会添加上下文，也不会改变 ChatGPT 可访问的内容；它只会改变项目或聊天在侧边栏中的位置。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>如需恢复已归档的聊天，请前往 <strong>Settings &gt; Data Controls &gt; Archived chats（设置 &gt; 数据控制 &gt; 已归档聊天）</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"use-local-projects-for-folders-and-codebases\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"_10\">使用本地项目管理文件夹和代码库</h2> <p>开启同步后，Work Cloud 会使用“本地计算机访问”协调云端的新任务；你可以在受支持的桌面、移动设备和网页体验中继续这些任务。对于企业，在功能发布初期，应用内的“本地/云端”开关及其默认值保持不变。现有任务（包括项目中的任务）仍只在本地运行，或在无法访问本地文件的云端运行。要使用此功能，请新建任务。</p> <p>如果新一轮开始时电脑不可用，符合条件且启用了 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问的现有任务可以在云端容器中继续运行。该容器无法访问这台电脑上的文件或工具，也无法强制执行企业运行要求。Work 不能在一轮任务执行过程中从本地切换到云端。</p> <p>对话同步和项目文件访问是两回事：</p> <ul> <li>同步对话不会上传整个本地文件夹，也不会让其他电脑访问该文件夹。</li> <li>继续任务时，请检查任务可以访问哪些来源和工具。</li> <li>Work 对话历史与 Codex 历史相互独立。</li> </ul> <p>如果 ChatGPT 需要读取或修改电脑上的文件，请添加本地项目。项目本身不一定要绑定文件夹；你可以按需附加文件夹。</p> <p>如需添加或更改文件夹，请打开项目菜单并选择 <strong>Edit project（编辑项目）</strong>。选择 <strong>Add folder（添加文件夹）</strong>即可附加多个文件夹。ChatGPT 可以读取和更改每个已附加文件夹中的文件。如需更改默认工作目录，请指向某个文件夹并选择 <strong>Make primary（设为主文件夹）</strong>。</p> <p>新聊天会从主文件夹开始。Codex 也会将其用作 Git 操作的默认目录，并从中自动发现 <code>AGENTS.md</code>、skills 和 <code>config.toml</code>。次要文件夹仍可用于搜索、读取和编辑文件，但 Codex 不会从次要文件夹自动发现这些项目配置文件。</p> <p>如果相关工作分散在不同位置，例如应用及其文档，或网站及其后端，可以使用多个文件夹。如果项目彼此无关，或每个聊天只应访问仓库的一部分，请创建不同项目。这样可以让工作上下文保持聚焦。远程项目目前只支持一个文件夹。</p> <p>使用<a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">本地环境</a>为项目定义设置操作和常用命令。<a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">审查面板</a>可以显示附加到同一项目的多个仓库中的变更。拉取请求和 <a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">worktree</a> 操作会针对主仓库。你在 worktree 中开始聊天时，其他文件夹仍会保持附加状态。</p> <p>项目和 worktree 可以整理工作，但<a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">沙箱</a>负责强制执行本地命令可以读取、修改或联网访问的范围。</p> <p><a id=\"start-without-a-project\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-a-task-without-a-project\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-chat-without-a-project\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">不使用项目开始聊天</h2> <p>在 Codex 中，选择 <strong>Recents（最近聊天）</strong>旁边的 <strong>New chat（新聊天）</strong>，即可不使用项目开始聊天。适用于无需共享项目文件、指令或文件夹访问权限的独立工作。如果多个聊天需要共用同一上下文，请先创建项目。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-a-task-without-a-project-1\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-chat-without-a-project_1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">不使用项目开始聊天</h2> <p>如果聊天不需要共享项目文件、指令或来源，就从 ChatGPT 主页开始聊天。你可以使用 Chat 或 ChatGPT Work；在网页上，两者都会创建聊天。</p> <p>如果工作范围扩大，可以把它移入项目，并为每个目标起一个清晰的聊天名称。一个项目可以并行安排研究、起草、审查和后续跟进等聊天，不必把所有内容混在一个上下文中。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-chat\"></a> <a id=\"start-a-standalone-chat\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-quick-chat-for-a-quick-conversation\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-quick-chat-for-a-quick-question\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">使用快速聊天进行简单交流</h2> <p>快速聊天会打开普通的 ChatGPT 聊天。ChatGPT 聊天不会显示在 Codex 侧边栏中；Codex 侧边栏只包含 Codex 聊天和项目。</p> <p>将鼠标指向 <strong>New chat（新聊天）</strong>，然后选择右侧的 <strong>Quick chat（快速聊天）</strong>图标。你也可以在 Windows 和 Linux 上按 <kbd>Ctrl+Alt+N</kbd>，或在 macOS 上按 <kbd>Cmd+Option+N</kbd>。从 <strong>New chat（新聊天）</strong>中还可以打开现有的 ChatGPT 聊天，并把它添加到 Codex 聊天中。</p> <p><a id=\"bring-in-other-tools-and-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_14\">引入其他工具和上下文</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>如果文件或<a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">图像输入</a>只与当前请求有关，可以直接将它们附加到聊天中。</li> <li>安装<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>，从其他服务引入上下文和操作能力。</li> <li>如果组织或开发环境通过 Model Context Protocol 提供工具，可以配置 <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> 服务器。</li> <li>在可用的情况下，使用<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>，让有用的上下文延续到后续聊天。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>只有当前请求需要时，才向聊天传入<a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">图像输入</a>。</li> <li>安装<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>，从其他服务引入上下文和操作能力。</li> <li>如果组织或开发环境通过 Model Context Protocol 提供工具，可以配置 <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> 服务器。</li> <li>在可用的情况下，使用<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>，让有用的上下文延续到后续聊天。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>当前轮次需要时，可引用已打开的文件，或在编辑器中选择代码来添加上下文。</li> <li>如果组织或开发环境通过 Model Context Protocol 提供工具，可以配置 <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> 服务器。</li> <li>如果连接的 Codex 主机提供<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>，可用它把有用的上下文延续到后续聊天。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>如果希望项目中的所有聊天都能使用某些文件和已连接来源，请将它们添加到项目的 <strong>Sources（来源）</strong>部分。</li> <li>只有当前请求需要时，才把文件或<a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">图像输入</a>直接附加到聊天中。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT Work 中，可安装<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>，从其他服务引入上下文和操作能力。</li> <li>在可用的情况下，使用<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>，让有用的上下文延续到后续聊天。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"next-steps\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">后续阅读</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">了解如何编写和改进提示词</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f\">了解如何使用 ChatGPT</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-916e12c5bba5b9cc\">继续长期运行的工作</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"projects-and-chats\">Projects and chats</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Use a project to organize related chats and give ChatGPT the context it needs. The <strong>Projects</strong> view in the ChatGPT desktop app includes ChatGPT projects and local projects that connect to folders on your computer.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-project-or-start-without-one\">Choose a project or start without one</h2> <p>Create a project when work will continue over time, produce more than one output, or depend on the same files and sources. Start a chat without a project when the work is self-contained and doesn't need shared project context.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Use a project to keep related chats, files, instructions, and sources together. The same project can contain chats started with Chat or ChatGPT Work.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-project-or-chat-without-one\">Choose a project or chat without one</h2> <p>Create a project when work will continue over time, produce more than one output, or depend on the same files and sources. Start a chat without a project when the work is self-contained and doesn't need shared project context.</p> <p>Each project has a <strong>Chats</strong> section that lists project chats and a <strong>Sources</strong> section for uploaded files and connected context. Project instructions apply across its chats. A ChatGPT project doesn't provide direct access to a folder on your computer, so upload or connect the sources you want ChatGPT to use.</p> <p>With either option, start a new chat from the project to use its shared files and instructions, then return to it under <strong>Chats</strong>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex CLI treats the directory where you start it as the project for the chat. Run <code>codex</code> from the directory you want Codex to work in, or pass <code>--cd &lt;directory&gt;</code> (<code>-C</code>) to set it explicitly. The CLI doesn't expose the ChatGPT Projects view.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The IDE extension treats the folder or workspace open in your IDE as the local project. In a multi-root workspace, select the workspace root for the chat. The extension doesn't expose the ChatGPT Projects view from the web or desktop app.</p> <p><a id=\"work-in-a-project\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"work-in-a-project\">Work in a project</h2> <p>The <strong>Projects</strong> view brings ChatGPT projects and local projects into one place. ChatGPT projects carry project files and context across related chats. A local project gives chats access to one or more folders on your computer, such as a collection of source files or a codebase.</p> <p>Start a separate chat for each distinct outcome so its messages and results stay focused while the project keeps related work organized.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app showing multiple projects in the sidebar and chats in the main pane</p> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"work-in-a-project_1\">Work in a project</h2> <p>A ChatGPT project gives its chats access to the same uploaded files, project instructions, and connected sources. Use Chat for a quick chat or ChatGPT Work for a larger deliverable; both appear as chats in the project's <strong>Chats</strong> section. Start a separate chat for each distinct outcome so its messages and results stay focused while the project preserves shared context.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"work-in-a-project-directory\">Work in a project directory</h2> <p>Start Codex from the directory that should provide the chat's file context. Use <code>/new</code> to start a separate chat for each distinct outcome. Use <code>/resume</code> while Codex is open, or run <code>codex resume</code>, to continue a saved chat.</p> <p>The chat keeps its transcript and recorded working directory, while Codex reads files from the current working tree. Keep durable project guidance in <code>AGENTS.md</code> or checked-in documentation so it is available to future chats.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"work-in-a-workspace\">Work in a workspace</h2> <p>Open the folder or workspace that should provide the chat's file context. Start a new chat for each distinct outcome, then select it from <strong>Recent chats</strong> to continue it. Chats in the same project can work with the same files, while each chat keeps its own transcript.</p> <p>The current selection and open files provide context for the current turn. Keep durable project guidance in <code>AGENTS.md</code> or checked-in documentation so it is available to future chats.</p> <p><a id=\"manage-project-threads\"></a> <a id=\"organize-projects-and-chats\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"organize-projects-and-tasks\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"organize-projects-and-chats\">Organize projects and chats</h2> <p>Keep active work visible and move finished work out of the way:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Pin a project</strong> to keep it near the top of the sidebar. You can also pin it from the Projects view.</li> <li><strong>Pin a chat</strong> when you return to it often, even if newer chats appear in the project.</li> <li><strong>Rename a chat</strong> with a short title that describes its outcome, such as “Q3 launch brief” or “Checkout accessibility review.”</li> <li><strong>Search projects</strong> from the Projects view. Open <strong>Search chats</strong> from the sidebar to find a past chat when you remember a phrase or branch name but not the title. Search chats doesn't have a default shortcut, but you can assign one under <strong>Settings &gt; Keyboard Shortcuts</strong>.</li> <li><strong>Archive a chat</strong> when you finish the work. From a project's menu, select <strong>Archive chats</strong> to archive its chats together.</li> </ul> <p>Pinning doesn't add context or change what ChatGPT can access. It only changes where the project or chat appears in the sidebar.</p> <p>Restore archived chats from <strong>Settings &gt; Archived chats</strong>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"organize-projects-and-tasks-1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"organize-projects-and-chats_1\">Organize projects and chats</h2> <p>Keep active work visible and move finished work out of the way:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Pin a project</strong> to keep it near the top of the sidebar. You can also pin it from the Projects view.</li> <li><strong>Pin a chat</strong> when you return to it often, even if newer chats appear in the project.</li> <li><strong>Rename a chat</strong> with a short title that describes its outcome, such as “Q3 launch brief” or “Checkout accessibility review.”</li> <li><strong>Search projects</strong> from the Projects view. Search past chats with <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> when you remember a phrase or branch name but not the title.</li> <li><strong>Archive a chat</strong> when you finish the work.</li> </ul> <p>Pinning doesn't add context or change what ChatGPT can access. It only changes where the project or chat appears in the sidebar.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Restore archived chats from <strong>Settings &gt; Data Controls &gt; Archived chats</strong>.</p> <p><a id=\"use-local-projects-for-folders-and-codebases\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"use-local-projects-for-folders-and-codebases\">Use local projects for folders and codebases</h2> <p>When sync is on, the cloud coordinates new tasks using Local computer access with Work Cloud, and you can continue them across supported desktop, mobile, and web experiences. For enterprises, the in-app Local/Cloud toggle and its default remain unchanged at launch. Existing tasks, including those in projects, stay local only or in the cloud without access to local files. Start a new task to use this feature.</p> <p>If your computer is unavailable when a new turn starts, an existing eligible task using Local computer access with Work Cloud can continue in a cloud container. The container can't access the computer's files or tools or enforce its enterprise execution requirements. Work can't switch from local to cloud execution during a turn.</p> <p>Conversation sync and project-file access are separate:</p> <ul> <li>Syncing a conversation doesn't upload the entire local folder or make it available to another computer.</li> <li>When you continue a task, review the sources and tools it can access.</li> <li>Work conversation history remains separate from Codex history.</li> </ul> <p>Add a local project when ChatGPT needs to read or change files on your computer. Projects don’t need a folder, but you can attach folders as needed.</p> <p>To add or change folders, open the project's menu and select <strong>Edit project</strong>. Select <strong>Add folder</strong> to attach multiple folders. ChatGPT can read and change files in every attached folder. To change the default working directory, point to a folder and select <strong>Make primary</strong>.</p> <p>New chats start in the primary folder. Codex also uses that folder as the default for Git operations and automatic discovery of <code>AGENTS.md</code>, skills, and <code>config.toml</code>. Secondary folders remain available for file search, reading, and editing, but Codex doesn't automatically discover those project files from secondary folders.</p> <p>Use multiple folders when related work lives in different places, like an app and its documentation or a website and its backend. Create separate projects for unrelated work or when each chat should access only one part of a repository. This keeps the working context focused. Remote projects currently support one folder.</p> <p>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">local environments</a> to define setup actions and common commands for a project. The <a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">review pane</a> can show changes across repositories attached to the same project. Pull request and <a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">worktree</a> actions target the primary repository. When you start a chat in a worktree, the other folders remain attached.</p> <p>Projects and worktrees organize work, but the <a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">sandbox</a> enforces what local commands can read, change, or access over the network.</p> <p><a id=\"start-without-a-project\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-a-task-without-a-project\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"start-a-chat-without-a-project\">Start a chat without a project</h2> <p>In Codex, select <strong>New chat</strong> beside <strong>Recents</strong> to start without a project. Use this for self-contained work that doesn't need shared project files, instructions, or folder access. Create a project first when several chats will depend on the same context.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-a-task-without-a-project-1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"start-a-chat-without-a-project_1\">Start a chat without a project</h2> <p>Start a chat from ChatGPT Home when the chat doesn't need shared project files, instructions, or sources. You can use Chat or ChatGPT Work; on the web, both create chats.</p> <p>If the work grows, move it into a project and use clear chat names for each outcome. A project can hold parallel chats for research, drafting, review, and follow-up without mixing every message into one context.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-chat\"></a> <a id=\"start-a-standalone-chat\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-quick-chat-for-a-quick-conversation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"use-quick-chat-for-a-quick-question\">Use Quick chat for a quick question</h2> <p>Quick chat opens an ordinary ChatGPT chat. ChatGPT chats don't appear in the Codex sidebar, which contains your Codex chats and projects.</p> <p>Point to <strong>New chat</strong>, then select the <strong>Quick chat</strong> icon on its right. You can also press</p> <p><kbd>Cmd+Option+N</kbd> on macOS or <kbd>Ctrl+Alt+N</kbd> on Windows and Linux. From <strong>New chat</strong>, you can open an existing ChatGPT chat and add it to a Codex chat.</p> <h2 id=\"bring-in-other-tools-and-context\">Bring in other tools and context</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>Attach files or <a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">image inputs</a> directly to a chat when they apply only to that request.</li> <li>Install <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a> to bring in context and actions from other services.</li> <li>Configure <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> servers when your organization or developer setup exposes tools through Model Context Protocol.</li> <li>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">memories</a>, where available, to carry useful context from past work into future chats.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>Pass <a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">image inputs</a> to a chat when visual context applies only to that request.</li> <li>Install <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a> to bring in context and actions from other services.</li> <li>Configure <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> servers when your organization or developer setup exposes tools through Model Context Protocol.</li> <li>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">memories</a>, where available, to carry useful context from past work into future chats.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>Reference open files or select code in the editor to add context for the current turn.</li> <li>Configure <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> servers when your organization or developer setup exposes tools through Model Context Protocol.</li> <li>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">memories</a> from the connected Codex host, where available, to carry useful context into future chats.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>Add files and connected sources to the project's <strong>Sources</strong> section when they should be available across its chats.</li> <li>Attach files or <a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">image inputs</a> directly to a chat when they apply only to that chat.</li> <li>In ChatGPT Work, install <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a> to bring in context and actions from other services.</li> <li>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">memories</a>, where available, to carry useful context from past work into future chats.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">Learn how to write and refine prompts</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f\">Learn how to use ChatGPT</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-916e12c5bba5b9cc\">Continue long-running work</a></li> </ul>"};
